# Coordinates are x,y with 0,0 top-left. docs/CURATED_SET.md §6 authors 'destroy 1,3' but its own D
# mark sits at 3,1 and the Warden sits directly beneath it — the board is authoritative (D-042).
#
# §6 also lands the Husk wave at 0,1 and 0,5, north of the wall. It cannot: a Destroy structure
# blocks its own tile, so `###D###` is a solid band and nothing north of it ever crosses. Authored
# as written the fight is an unwinnable stalemate from round 3, because the bodies you are told to
# use as ammunition are sealed on the wrong side of the door (D-046). The wave comes round the
# flank instead, onto the players' side, where it can be shoved.
#
#   .  open        #  wall        O  pit        ^  spikes      H  high ground
#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot       D  the destroy structure

id: break-the-gate
number: 6
name: Break the Gate
description: An eight-hit-point gate that only collisions can dent, and a Warden holding the gap who becomes your battering ram the moment he is staggered.
design: docs/CURATED_SET.md §1 fight 6 — Destroy. The review's worst opener, reborn.
design: The gate is an 8 HP structure that attacks cannot touch at all. The only thing that hurts it is a collision — 2 per slam, four slams — so to win you have to throw bodies at it, which means the enemy is your ammunition. That is the game's thesis stated as a win condition.
design: The Warden under the gate is the complication: Move 0, so unlike the Anchors it replaced it will still be standing in the gap on round 4. It is push-resistant, but a STAGGERED Warden moves — so collide a Husk from the reinforcement waves into him and he becomes the battering ram.

spawn l = Lobber
spawn w = Warden
spawn h = Husk

roster a: Vanguard, Threadcaster
roster b: Wardbearer, Archer

objective: destroy 3,1

wave 2 = h@0,3 h@6,3

board:
  .l...l.
  ###D###
  ..^w^..
  ...H...
  .......
  A.....B
  AA...BB
